  clock: 11  # b778
  nonce: b778  # b778
  message: "PRODUCER RECONCILIATION landed in PR c9b6240701 (ADR-0035 §3, stays scheme v6 per §6). Two post-linker passes: split_within_file_stable_id_collisions (SITE occurrence-index, :occ:<n> re-hash) + dedup_logical_synthetic_identities (message_queue/event_sourcing LOGICAL dedup to one hub, edges rewired). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (self-tree re-measure via run_behavior_map, 35080 nodes): per-file stable_id collision groups 35 -> 0 (the ADR-0035 §5 HARD per-file uniqueness gate is now CLEAN on the real corpus); corpus-wide collisions 43->14 groups, 149->37 symbols (0.43% -> 0.1%). Adversarially reviewed (4 dims, skeptic-verified); only confirmed finding was a graphql allowlist over-inclusion (graphql protocol_origin shared by resolver fields + client call-sites), fixed by excluding graphql from the LOGICAL set so client sites are not collapsed. STATUS: the per-file HARD limb of this META is MET; the corpus-rate limb is NOT yet ~0 — the residual 14 are a distinct mechanism (same-named top-level tree-sitter symbols, e.g. bash usage() across scripts, whose hash omits file identity — the INV-zudob class for tree-sitter, never folded for the BaseAnalyzer path) filed as WI-bokab (fix = fold file identity into tree-sitter top-level containing_stable_id, a corpus-wide rehash needing a scheme-bump decision). Stays pending_validation + awaits_bakeoff_validation until WI-bokab closes the corpus limb and a bakeoff confirms the collision-rate movement."  # b778
